<title>BELGIUM: COREPER to discuss cattle imports.</title>
<headline>COREPER to discuss cattle imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>COREPER will shortly discuss discuss imports of live cattle into the EU after the Commission said that shipments from eastern Europe and from other suppliers must be on the same basis, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Under the GATT Uruguay Round agreement, the EU agreed to import from all countries 169,000 head of cattle in 1997 at a reduced tariff rate of 16 percent plus 582 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>But last month the EU agreed to import 500,000 tonnes of cattle in 1997 at a 16 percent tariff reduction plus 399 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>The Commission says that the same import terms should apply to eastern European and other cattle exporters in order to conform with World Trade Organisation rules.</p>
</text>
